    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): Both proposals relied only on the one-line note [ev-e4380102a652]. The linked PR fills in the details. It says installing a provider package that references a DeploymentRuntimeConfig was \"currently broken on main\", shown with a dev build tagged v1.21.0-rc.0.163 [ev-2955a2390de6]. The provider revision went unhealthy because applying the Deployment failed with duplicate volumeMount paths \"/tls/client\" and \"/tls/server\" that \"must be unique\" [ev-a95dca88b623]. The fix is a DeepCopy of the runtime config's Deployment template spec in internal/controller/pkg/runtime/runtime_defaults.go [ev-c8ee24a21df6]. That is enough to write the assertion: subject = the provider Deployment built from a DeploymentRuntimeConfig; change = bug fix; applicability = provider packages that reference a DeploymentRuntimeConfig; consequence = none for operators, since the PR describes a regression on unreleased main that this release fixes.",
